in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl

# @mirror/spectral — the agent coordination layer.
#
# The recognition (2026-06-06, Alex + Mara → Pack): the substrate has
# been operating a multi-agent orchestra for weeks. The Pack — Reed,
# Mara, Glint, Taut, Seam, and future voices — has been coordinating
# through stigmergic traces on the eigenboard, kintsugi oscillation,
# Fate auditions, and consent boundaries that were tribal knowledge
# until they had a name. This family declares the discipline.
#
# Load-bearing spec: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md (commit a8055f0).
# Memory: [[project-pack-is-orchestra]].
#
# === The orchestra ===
#
# Voices (agents): Reed, Mara, Glint, Taut, Seam — and future voices.
# Sections: shard subtrees on which a voice has authoring authority.
# Score: the eigenboard + the metalogue + the kintsugi loop's pending
#        state.
# Conductor: the refract lens, read between oscillation passes; a
#            *role* that rotates per tick, not a permanent agent.
# Audition: the Fate tournament, wearing its orchestra name.
# Voice-leading: the kintsugi-tournament strategy vocabulary (per
#                docs/specs/kintsugi-tournament.md).
# Harmonic progression: the path through the K_n attractor.
# Holonomy: the closure of an oscillation round (zero = coherent).
# Resolution: e^(n+1) < e^n; the loop closes.
#
# === Discipline ===
#
# A `@mirror/spectral` instance IS:
#
#   - an oscillator: kintsugi alternates ACTIVE/DARK passes (per the
#     SpectralUuid duality). The bi-directional gradient computes from
#     each pending crack forward AND from each export backward; the
#     intersection picks the next focus. The substrate either has
#     uniqueness (auto-apply) or it doesn't (consent surface).
#   - a coordination layer: voices play their sections; the conductor
#     reads refract; the score is the eigenboard envelope plus the
#     metalogue bus plus pending kintsugi state. Stigmergic, not
#     command-and-control.
#   - a consent contract: the loss-decreasing-vs-trade-off boundary
#     IS structural, not policy. Loss-decreasing morphisms with unique
#     winners auto-apply; pareto-fronts pause for the next consent
#     surface (Alex, a higher-temperature Fate tournament, an explicit
#     human signal).
#
# === Species under this family ===
#
# Form-side species (THIS family — @mirror/spectral declares the
# orchestra's OBSERVATION surface; voices and sections read these):
#
#   @mirror/spectral/conductor  the refract-reader role. The conductor
#                                signal is a tournament_outcome-shaped
#                                trace on the eigenboard; the role
#                                rotates per tick.
#   @mirror/spectral/voice      peer-as-agent with named authority
#                                over zero or more sections; ties
#                                identity to a content-addressed
#                                @peer/identity declaration.
#   @mirror/spectral/section    shard subtree under a voice's
#                                authority; cross-section writes
#                                require an oscillation pause.
#   @mirror/spectral/score      eigenboard envelope + metalogue bus +
#                                pending kintsugi state, named
#                                collectively as the score. Read-only
#                                to voices; mutated through the
#                                convergence.
#   @mirror/spectral/audition   Fate tournament wearing its orchestra
#                                name. @fate.minimize is the resolver;
#                                the audition declaration is naming,
#                                not invention.
#   @mirror/spectral/portal     typed transport over a content-addressed
#                                subspace; portal-as-eigenvalue-stream-
#                                as-gen_prism per the 26th-instance
#                                `shift(oid, T)` recognition (Reed
#                                2026-06-08; docs/insights/2026-06-08-
#                                portal-eigenvalue-stream-gen-prism.md).
#                                Four fields (socket, subspace, frame,
#                                actor — three carrying `shift(oid, T)`);
#                                project_eigenvalue as the focus
#                                projection at the transport altitude.
#                                Sub-species handshake/codec/stream at
#                                `shards/mirror/spectral/portal/`. Lifted
#                                from the boot floor `boot/std/spectral/
#                                portal*` (retained as transitional
#                                placeholder during consumer-pull
#                                migration). Third tick of the 5-tick
#                                cascade closing the pretty-printer LRM.
#
# Process-side species (MIGRATED 2026-06-10 to @kintsugi per the
# form/process partition; recognition #55 candidate). These species
# were originally declared under @mirror/spectral; the family-root
# migration moved them to @kintsugi where they belong (transformation
# engine vs orchestra observation surface). Form-side species above
# still reference them at the import altitude (score consumes
# @kintsugi/oscillate and @kintsugi/consent; portal still consumes
# @mirror/spectral at the family root). Cross-family references:
#
#   @kintsugi/oscillate         the loop primitive; kintsugi's
#                                heartbeat. ACTIVE/DARK alternation;
#                                tick chain; holonomy; eigenvalue
#                                frequency. The load-bearing one.
#                                Migrated from @mirror/spectral/
#                                oscillate.
#   @kintsugi/consent           the auto-apply boundary. Declares the
#                                pareto-front / unique-winner split
#                                that governs when oscillation pauses
#                                for a next-consent-surface signal.
#                                Migrated from @mirror/spectral/
#                                consent.
#   @kintsugi/morphism          the typed pre/post-morphism pair. Lifts
#                                consent's per-candidate `morphism`
#                                carrier by adding the `pre_anchor: ref`
#                                field so identity_preserving's DARK-
#                                bits comparison is self-contained at
#                                the per-candidate altitude; the
#                                substrate's per-candidate slice of the
#                                eigenboard.context. Migrated from
#                                @mirror/spectral/morphism.
#
# Forward-references only — form-side sub-shards land as consumers
# pull them. Process-side migration to @kintsugi is closed this tick;
# see `shards/kintsugi.mirror` for the migrated family root.
#
# === Sibling relationship to @mirror/lens ===
#
# `@mirror/lens` observes; `@mirror/spectral` coordinates. The two are
# *siblings* at the mirror altitude — neither contains the other; both
# project the same five-operation algebra through their own typed
# surface. The lens family IS the orchestra's observation sections
# (cli/shell/mcp/lsp see the substrate; transit/refract measure it).
# The spectral family consumes lens — the conductor reads refract;
# voices read transit — but the dependency points only one way at the
# sub-shard altitude, not at the family root. Family roots stay
# decoupled so consumers can pull species independently.
#
# Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]: `prism
# @mirror/spectral { ... }` declares the family IS a prism. The
# five-operation block below is the canonical declaration form (cf.
# shards/mirror/lens.mirror, shards/code.mirror). Each sub-shard
# specialises from there.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md (the full proposal;
#               commit a8055f0),
#               docs/specs/kintsugi-tournament.md (voice-leading and
#               audition vocabulary),
#               docs/specs/the-convergence.md (the lens-family
#               sibling; four transports + two measurements),
#               docs/specs/trace-kintsugi-pipeline.md (refract as the
#               conductor's ear).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]],
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the oscillation
#                      ascends the bounded semilattice).
# Related shards: mirror/lens.mirror (the sibling family; observation
#                 to spectral's coordination),
#                 mirror/spec.mirror (the spec discipline; spectral
#                 instances declare specs through here),
#                 mirror/au.mirror (au = proposed, settled into shard;
#                 voices emit au; the score keeps shards).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/spectral.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/spectral` as the family root; species live at
# `shards/mirror/spectral/<name>.mirror`.

out @mirror/spectral
